AABCmtIsQ","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-17T07:37:35Z","updated_at":"2026-05-17T09:47:33Z","body":"> Hello maintainers, I would like to work on this WASAPI capture issue. I will first determine whether the silent capture can be reproduced or isolated through the Windows audio capture path, then add diagnostics and a targeted fix for the failing microphone stream handling. Please assign this to me if appropriate.\n\nGodot does not assign people to work on issues. I'm not aware of anyone working on a fix at the moment, so you can work on it yourself.\nPlease remember to follow the rules and guidelines for pull requests, which can be found here: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4469770417/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5233432433","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119498#issuecomment-5233432433","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119498","id":5233432433,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN-_XcQ","user":{"login":"goatchurchprime","id":677254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime","html_url":"https://github.com/goatchurchprime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T19:24:17Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T19:24:17Z","body":"I'm not able to reproduce this.  ie when I tried recording and playing back with the mic_record app (the sound going through a steam link to the a VR headset), the playback of my voice was heard.  (There was no problem with the [mix_input](https://github.com/goatchurchprime/godot-demo-projects/tree/gtch/mic_input/audio/mic_input) demo either.)\n\nI'd installed and enabled that StealSeries Sonar app, where you can drag the Godot app into the columns where it gives the 7.1 surround sound mode.  To my surprise, the Godot editor updates the number of mono channels from 2 to 8 while it is running.\n \n<img width=\"1337\" height=\"768\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/208b0bff-294a-4951-959e-751296a69fb6\" />\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1017\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f4e05acc-76d5-4a85-b65a-698d342173e8\" />\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5233432433/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5242407229","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119498#issuecomment-5242407229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119498","id":5242407229,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOHjJPQ","user":{"login":"LingLambda","id":101567686,"node_id":"U_kgDOBg3Mxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101567686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda","html_url":"https://github.com/LingLambda","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-10T15:32:14Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T15:32:14Z","body":"@goatchurchprime, thank you very much for testing this!\n\nI retested the `mic_record` project on my computer. I am using the latest SteelSeries Sonar version, `116.0.0`. When I start the project, my Sonar interface looks like this:\n\n<img width=\"1708\" height=\"958\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/525de6e6-ec3e-4a02-8bf1-fa73d1242b9e\" />\n\nJust as before, `mic_record` is unable to capture any audio data.\n\nHowever, I also tried the `mix_input` demo you mentioned. To my surprise, microphone input works correctly there: it receives my voice, displays the waveform, and plays it back properly. Perhaps this is because it uses `AudioServer.get_input_frames()`? I will investigate further and try to provide useful additional information.\n\nI also noticed that Sonar does not appear to be configured as the default audio device in your screenshot, which might prevent it from working fully. You could try clicking **\"Click to auto set defaults\"**. This may not persist, meaning that the warning could reappear, because applications such as Steam Link or Virtual Desktop can take over Windows' default input and output devices.\n\nThe best test might be to connect the microphone directly to the computer, click **\"Click to auto set defaults\"**, make sure the warning no longer appears, and then test again.\n\nAlso, Godot does indeed switch to 8 channels when Sonar starts. I had not noticed this before because I always kept Sonar enabled. Only after you mentioned it did I disable Sonar and notice the difference.\n\nFinally, thank you again to all the maintainers for your hard work!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5242407229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5242799342","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119498#issuecomment-5242799342","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119498","id":5242799342,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOH7E7g","user":{"login":"LingLambda","id":101567686,"node_id":"U_kgDOBg3Mxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101567686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda","html_url":"https://github.com/LingLambda","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingLambda/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-10T16:06:47Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T16:08:04Z","body":"Okay, I've basically confirmed it: when I changed the audio capture in mic_record to use AudioServer.get_input_frames_available(), it worked almost perfectly.\n\n<img width=\"1871\" height=\"922\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/222951a5-ae98-4d58-8eb4-56885dfce495\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5242799342/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5370471224","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119498#issuecomment-5370471224","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119498","id":5370471224,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQBrjOA","user":{"login":"Jaytheway","id":22476284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDc2Mjg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22476284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway","html_url":"https://github.com/Jaytheway","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-21T13:36:38Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T13:41:21Z","body":"Looks like Sonar creates 7.1 virtual device, which means we get 4 instances of `AudioEffectRecordInstance`, but only the last one is stored in `AudioEffectRecord` as `current_instance`. That last one supposedly corresponds to the last two channels of the virtual Sonar device, which can be silent.\nMeaning whatever you see going through the last two volume meter bars on the Godot buses, is what's going into the recorded file.\n\nThis should be fixed by #92532","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5370471224/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]